1
00:06:26,666 --> 00:06:32,666
Now is the time for heroes.

2
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:59,333
Escape to Victory is a drama, war film directed by John Huston.

3
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:26,000
A group of POWs in a German prison camp during World War II play the German National Soccer
Team in this powerful film depicting the role of prisoners during wartime.

4
00:25:46,666 --> 00:25:52,666
Captain Robert Hatch, played by Sylvester Stallone.

5
00:32:13,333 --> 00:32:19,333
Captain John Colby, played by Michael Caine.

6
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Major Karl von Steiner, played by Max von Sydow.

7
00:45:06,666 --> 00:45:12,666
Cpl. Luis Fernandez, Brazil, played by Pelé.

8
00:51:33,333 --> 00:51:39,333
Renée, played by Carole Laure.

9
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Terry Brady, England, played by Bobby Moore.

10
01:04:26,666 --> 01:04:32,666
Escape to Victory (or simply Victory) is a 1981 sports war film directed by John Huston
and starring Sylvester Stallone, Michael Caine, Max von Sydow and Pelé.

11
01:10:53,333 --> 01:10:59,333
The film is about Allied prisoners of war who are interned in a German prison camp during the
Second World War who play an exhibition match of football against a German team.

12
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
The film received great attention upon its theatrical release, as it starred professional footballers Bobby Moore,
Osvaldo Ardiles, Kazimierz Deyna, Paul Van Himst, Mike Summerbee, Hallvar Thoresen, Werner Roth and Pelé.

13
01:23:46,666 --> 01:23:52,666
Numerous Ipswich Town players were also in the film, including John Wark,
Russell Osman, Laurie Sivell, Robin Turner and Kevin O'Callaghan.

14
01:30:13,333 --> 01:30:19,333
Other Ipswich Town players stood in for actors in the football scenes – Kevin
Beattie for Michael Caine, and Paul Cooper for Sylvester Stallone.

15
01:36:40,000 --> 01:36:46,000
Yabo Yablonsky wrote the script and the film was entered into
the 12th Moscow International Film Festival.

16
01:43:06,666 --> 01:43:12,666
The film explores themes of nazi, escape, sports, football (soccer).

17
01:49:33,333 --> 01:49:39,333
The tone is emotional.
